@description REAPER MCP — Model Context Protocol interface (immersive/spatial audio)
@version 1.13.3
@author James Livingston
@link https://github.com/inseglet-audio/inseglet
@provides
  [darwin] reaper_mcp.dylib https://github.com/inseglet-audio/inseglet/releases/download/v$version/reaper_mcp.dylib
@changelog
  A mutating tool now reports the input it silently adjusted.

  `track.set_channels` clamps a request below 2 up to 2, clamps above 64 down to 64, and rounds an
  odd count upward -- and it returned `{"ok": true, "channels": N}` with nothing naming any of it, so
  a caller that trusted `ok` could not see that it had not been given what it asked for. It now
  returns `clamped` and a `warnings` line naming what was asked and what was set, both declared in
  its output schema. Nothing about the adjustment itself changed.

  The reporting shape is the one this binary already shipped elsewhere: `warnings` as the `spatial.*`
  tools use it, `clamped` as the accessor tools declare it. Fifteen other mutating tools still adjust
  their inputs silently and are unchanged here.

  Surface 190 tools / 4 resources / 5 prompts -- UNMOVED. ctest 28 -> 29, one added.
